args.description:
List of command-line arguments to prepend to xdelta3 invocations via the XDELTA environment variable. Items correspond to documented options like -S, -s, -d, etc. Each item is a single string representing one argument or key-value pair (e.g. '-S djw', '-s source.tar.gz'). For multi-word arguments, they should be split into separate list items if the shell expansion semantics require it, but typically XDELTA is a single space-separated string. To simplify, each list item represents a segment. However, since XDELTA is a single env var string, we join these with spaces. To allow flexibility for options that take values, we structure each item as a string that can be joined. A better approach for a config file is to provide a list of key-value pairs or a single string. Given the constraint of Jinja2 filters, we'll use a list of strings that will be joined with spaces to form the XDELTA value. Example: ['-S', 'djw', '-s', 'source.tar.gz'] joins to '-S djw -s source.tar.gz'.
      items: {
        type: string,
        default: '',
        description: 'An argument segment for the XDELTA environment variable.'
      }
    }
  },
